{"id": "qa-001", "category": "qa", "question": "What is chickenpox and how is it also known?", "ground_truth": "Chickenpox, also called varicella, is a common and extremely infectious childhood disease that produces an itchy, blistery rash typically lasting about a week.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Chickenpox", "tags": ["definition", "infectious"]}
{"id": "qa-002", "category": "qa", "question": "Why are antibiotics not used to treat chickenpox?", "ground_truth": "Because chickenpox is a viral disease, antibiotics are ineffective against it; treatment focuses on reducing discomfort and fever.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Chickenpox/Treatment", "tags": ["treatment", "viral"]}
{"id": "qa-003", "category": "qa", "question": "What is cirrhosis?", "ground_truth": "Cirrhosis is a chronic, degenerative disease in which normal liver cells are damaged and replaced by scar tissue.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Cirrhosis", "tags": ["definition", "liver"]}
{"id": "qa-004", "category": "qa", "question": "What causes a cold sore?", "ground_truth": "A cold sore is a fluid-filled blister that usually appears at the edge of the lips, caused by a herpes simplex virus infection.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Cold sore", "tags": ["cause", "viral"]}
{"id": "qa-005", "category": "qa", "question": "What is the key symptom of croup?", "ground_truth": "Croup arises from a viral infection of the larynx and its key symptom is a harsh barking cough; most children recover within a few days.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Croup", "tags": ["symptom", "childhood"]}
{"id": "qa-006", "category": "qa", "question": "How is diabetes mellitus defined?", "ground_truth": "Diabetes mellitus is a condition in which the pancreas no longer produces enough insulin, or cells stop responding to insulin, so glucose in the blood cannot be absorbed into the body's cells.", "expected_behavior": "answer", "source": "Gale: Diabetes mellitus", "tags": ["definition", "endocrine"]}
